{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואומר אלכם", :translit "v'omar aleichem", :gloss "And I said to you"} {:he "חסר יו\"ד", :translit "chaseir yud", :gloss "defective (of) yod"} {:he "י\"פ הוכיחם", :translit "yud p'am hochichem", :gloss "ten times He admonished them"} {:he "י\"פ כתיב מיתת משה בתורה", :translit "yud p'am katuv mitat Moshe baTorah", :gloss "ten times the death of Moses is written in the Torah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The word ואומר is written defectively (without a second yod), and the count of ten connects to two separate enumerations."}], :frame {:text "The Midrash records ten occasions on which Moses was admonished (Sifrei Devarim 1; Devarim Rabbah 1:1). The tradition that the death of Moses is written ten times in the Torah refers to repeated divine pronouncements of Moses' impending death (cf. Numbers 27:13, Deuteronomy 1:37, 3:26, 4:21–22, 31:2, 31:14, 31:16, 32:50, 33:1, 34:5).", :sources ["Sifrei Devarim 1" "Devarim Rabbah 1:1" "Numbers 27:13" "Deuteronomy 1:37" "Deuteronomy 3:26" "Deuteronomy 4:21" "Deuteronomy 31:2" "Deuteronomy 31:14" "Deuteronomy 32:50" "Deuteronomy 34:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The word ואומר is written defectively (without a second yod), and the count of ten connects to two separate enumerations.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:33:23.509930513Z", :model "glm-5.2"}